[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Flaky Test Identification, Retries, and Performance Optimization in Cypress"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Flaky tests are tests that can pass and fail under the same conditions, undermining trust in CI/CD pipelines. This tutorial covers strategies to identify flakiness, configure smart retries, and optimize performance in Cypress."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Understanding and Identifying Flaky Tests"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Flakiness usually stems from network latency, asynchronous state updates, unhandled animations, or test isolation issues. To identify flaky tests effectively, leverage Cypress Cloud analytics or use local rerun plugins to execute tests multiple times."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Configuring Retries in Cypress"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Cypress allows you to configure test retries globally or per test suite. While retries help mask intermittent failures in CI, they should not be used as a permanent fix for inherently unstable code."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"describe('User Login Suite', { retries: { runMode: 2, openMode: 0 } }, () => {
  it('should log in successfully', () => {
    cy.visit('/login');
    cy.get('#username').type('test_user');
    cy.get('#password').type('secure_password');
    cy.get('#submit').click();
    cy.url().should('include', '/dashboard');
  });
});"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Eliminating Anti-Patterns Causing Flakiness"},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Avoid using arbitrary hardcoded waits like cy.wait(5000). Instead, wait for network aliases or DOM assertions."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure test isolation by resetting state before each test using beforeEach hooks and API commands."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Rely on Cypress automatic retry-assertion mechanism rather than custom conditional logic."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Performance Optimization Techniques"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"To speed up test execution, minimize UI interactions by seeding data via API requests before loading the page. Additionally, disable unnecessary video recordings and screenshots in CI if they are not needed."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"// cypress.config.js
const { defineConfig } = require('cypress');

module.exports = defineConfig({
  e2e: {
    video: false,
    screenshotOnRunFailure: true,
    defaultCommandTimeout: 6000,
    setupNodeEvents(on, config) {
      // implement node event listeners here
    },
  },
});"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining robust locators, explicit network waiting, smart retry configurations, and API-driven test setups, you can drastically reduce flakiness and improve overall test execution performance in Cypress."}]
